status: 400
request: GET http://myvariant.info/v1/query?q=snpeff.ann.effect:missense_variant%20AND%20dbnsfp.uniprot.acc:&fields=_id&fetch_all=true

Probed 2026-09-16 against upstream:

  400  656 bytes  {"code":400,"success":false,"error":"search_phase_execution_exception",
                  "root_cause_line_00":"parse_exception: Encountered '<EOF>' at line 1, column 58."...}

The same query with a trailing ")" instead is also 400 (953
bytes, column 64), and with a nonsense-but-well-formed
accession (NOSUCHACC) it is 200 with an empty hit list -- so
the 400 is the parser refusing the query, not upstream
refusing the accession, and it is stable under both.
